      "feedback": "This is an outstanding first-cut! Introducing a lesser-known New Guinea native like Ptychosperma schefferi (Scheffer’s Palm) represents the exact type of high-utility, specialized horticulture that makes Palma Sola's collection so respected.To elevate this profile to our established peer-reviewed standards, our editorial pass resolves your three flagged areas of uncertainty with precise botanical, historical, and physiological evidence.🔍 Key Botanical & Historical Corrections1. The Namesake Mystery Solved (Scheffer's Legacy)The Fact: The palm was indeed named in honor of Rudolf Herman Christiaan Carel Scheffer (1844–1880), a prominent Dutch botanist and director of the Bogor (Buitenzorg) Botanical Gardens in Java.The Connection: Legendary Italian botanist Odoardo Beccari described the species from specimens cultivated at Bogor during or shortly after Scheffer's tenure. We can confidently drop the \"possibly\" caveat and frame this as a direct historical tribute.2. The Fruit & Foliage Saf",
